    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0131" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/8304: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-18T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 18,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9366. Referring your No. 1813 of December 16, 11 p.m.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d35-f1"/> You should make sure that representatives on Council of
                    Heads of Delegations understand fully that United States is not to be considered
                    as party to any resolution, declaration, or action of or by the Council unless
                    through special act of the Department this Government expressly adheres thereto,
                    since you are taking part in the work of the Council as observer only.</p>
                <p>Because the Austrian treaty has not been put before the United States Senate,
                    this Government is at present not able to take action upon the Supreme Council’s
                    resolution concerning Vorarlberg, although unnumbered telegram from you received
                    December 17<anchor n="16" xml:id="d35-f2"/> seems to indicate that before
                    instructions requested in your 1813, December 16, could arrive action had been
                    taken upon said resolution.</p>
                <p>Will you please inform me if Council understands fully this state of affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
